  "rationales": {
    "U": "证据片段：'It should be used' – 因为代词'it'没有明确指代，使得需求难以理解。",
    "A": "证据片段：'It should be used' and 'formalization of the software' – 'it'指代不明，'formalization'含义模糊，引入歧义。",
    "C": "证据片段：整个句子 – 需求没有指定主体或上下文，使得其正确性依赖于未陈述的假设。",
    "V": "证据片段：'should be used' – 这是一个非可测试的陈述，没有提供验证标准或可衡量指标。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "改写为：'The software requirements specification shall be used by software engineers during development.'",
    "A": "改写为：使用具体术语，指定'it'为'requirements specification'，并澄清'formalization'为'formalized requirements'。",
    "C": "改写为：添加上下文，例如'此需求适用于软件需求文档的用途描述'。",
    "V": "改写为：使其可验证，例如'软件工程师应记录每次使用需求文档的开发活动'。"
  },
  "issues": [
    {
      "type": "U",
      "evidence": "It should be used",
      "rewrite": "Software engineers shall use the software requirements specification during development. The specification shall formalize the software to be delivered to clients/users."
    },
    {
      "type": "A",
      "evidence": "It should be used and formalization of the software",
      "rewrite": "Software engineers shall use the software requirements specification during development. The specification shall formalize the software to be delivered to clients/users."
    },
    {
      "type": "C",
      "evidence": "It should be used by software engineers who will develop this piece of software and it should be used for formalization of the software that is going to be delivered to clients/users.",
      "rewrite": "Software engineers shall use the software requirements specification during development. The specification shall formalize the software to be delivered to clients/users."
    },
    {
      "type": "V",
      "evidence": "should be used",
      "rewrite": "Software engineers shall use the software requirements specification during development. The specification shall formalize the software to be delivered to clients/users."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'It should be used by software engineers' and 'it should be used for formalization of the software' lack subject clarity — 'it' is ambiguous (referent undefined), and 'formalization' is jargon without definition; readers cannot reliably infer who uses what for which purpose.","A":"'Software engineers who will develop this piece of software' is vague: no criteria for identifying such engineers (e.g., role, access level, training); 'the software that is going to be delivered to clients/users' conflates delivery scope (client vs. end user) and lacks temporal specificity ('going to be' is non-binding future tense).","C":"The statement describes usage intent but does not contradict known domain facts; however, it omits essential context (e.g., what artifact 'it' refers to — requirements spec? model? DSL?) making correctness assessment incomplete — yet no internal logical contradiction exists, so score is moderate.","V":"No testable condition is present: 'should be used' is normative and unobservable; no measurable action, actor role verification, output artifact, or success criterion (e.g., 'must appear in at least two design review minutes', 'shall be cited in the SRS section 4.2') is provided — thus fundamentally unverifiable."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with atomic, subject-explicit statement naming the artifact and its users.","A":"Define 'software engineers' as 'developers assigned to the Project X implementation team, holding Role ID DEV-2024 or higher, and having completed Requirement Modeling Training v3.1'; define 'software' as 'the executable system described in System Boundary Document SB-2024-001'.","C":"Keep unchanged — no factual error detected, but requires upstream clarification of 'it' (e.g., R0 must define the artifact).","V":"Replace with a behaviorally observable and auditable requirement."},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"It should be used by software engineers who will develop this piece of software","rewrite":"The Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document shall be provided to all developers assigned to the Project X implementation team prior to Sprint 1 planning."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"software engineers who will develop this piece of software","rewrite":"Developers assigned to the Project X implementation team, holding Role ID DEV-2024 or higher, and having completed Requirement Modeling Training v3.1"},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"it should be used for formalization of the software that is going to be delivered to clients/users","rewrite":"The SRS document shall contain a traceable mapping from each functional requirement to at least one corresponding use case in the Use Case Specification UC-2024-001, verified by signature of the Lead Architect and dated before the System Design Review."}
  ]
}
